From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 09:43:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08046/11362] No endpoint closer than banked levels can carry
 the induce intervention -- and the 12-game corpus cannot localize where the
 chain breaks

The follow-on to the Phase-3 refusal (4609ac040) asked for the cheapest VALID
endpoint between the repeat_penalty induce intervention and banked levels. There
is none, and the reason is a design limit rather than a measurement.

The live corpus is 12 games of which 2 bank any level. With those margins a
two-sided Fisher test can reach p<0.05 ONLY if the predictor is positive in 2, 3,
9 or 10 games. Every stage true of 4-8 games is UNDECIDABLE BY CONSTRUCTION. The
only predictors that clear the bar are the post-bank stages (goal-satisfiable,
plan-found), which are consequences of banking rather than causes of it. So
"only reverse-causal stages predict" is guaranteed by the design, not discovered.

Every (b) row now carries its min reachable p, matching what Phase 1 already did
for the (a) paired tests. Withdrawn as unsupported: "no stage passes both (a) and
(b)"; "correctness is certainly not positive"; and the force-admit trace-identity
argument (all 10 matched pairs have plan_length=0 in the admit arm, so identical
traces are mechanically entailed -- and vc33, the only game with dynamic range,
has zero admit cells). The stronger honest form of the force-admit result is that
where it DID produce real plans (lengths 61 and 6) levels_gained was still 0.

Reinstated: S7 (held-out accuracy > 0) as the surviving mediator candidate. It
responds (p=0.0386, floor 0.0005) and both banking games sit inside it -- the
maximum association a group of 7 permits. Its (b) evidence sits at the n=12
ceiling (floor 0.1515); it was never refuted. If S7 mediates, banked levels costs
34 cells against the refusal's 68. Whether it mediates needs a corpus with more
bankable games (n>=36 at the observed rate), not more cells at n=12.

The endpoint is floored: three independent manipulations -- engine retention
on/off, the whole LLM tier on/off, and force-admitting the trust gate -- moved
banked levels exactly zero times. Absent any movable condition, every per-stage
"does not predict" verdict is untestable rather than tested.

Correct engines per GPU-hour: usable/GPU-h is a real 2.60x gain surviving all
three tests (Poisson p=0.0055, paired sign p=0.0025, game-cluster bootstrap CI
[2.13,6.75]). Strict-quality/GPU-h fails all three, and the non-vacuous count is
identical 4 vs 4 -- the ratio is entirely denominator.

Banked levels remain 3/3 and the submission gate is UNMET. No GPU was used, no
scored or online game was played, nothing was submitted, and no existing artifact
was modified.

